1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:02,469
Ah, you want to talk about my wife?

2
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:14,814
The best, really.

3
00:00:14,814 --> 00:00:20,887
Very supportive wife,
very patient, all love.

4
00:00:21,654 --> 00:00:24,791
When she gets mad, nothing.

5
00:00:24,924 --> 00:00:27,527
No matter what I do, nothing.

6
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,662
She just looks at me, like this, see?

7
00:00:31,664 --> 00:00:34,334
- What?
- Mm, see? Right?

8
00:00:34,359 --> 00:00:36,594
When she looks at you
like that, you just stay quiet.

9
00:00:37,303 --> 00:00:38,226
Right?

10
00:00:38,638 --> 00:00:39,447
One more time.

11
00:00:39,472 --> 00:00:40,607
See? Nothing.

12
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:42,308
I didn’t say anything.

13
00:00:42,342 --> 00:00:43,743
No, you’re the best.

14
00:00:43,777 --> 00:00:45,345
- One more time.
- Nothing, I didn’t say anything.

15
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:46,246
Say it.

16
00:00:46,746 --> 00:00:47,555
I’m the best?

17
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:48,796
Yes, absolutely! Super.

18
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:50,483
Okay, very good.

19
00:01:51,478 --> 00:01:54,047
Andres is very sweet.

20
00:01:57,250 --> 00:01:59,486
She always has jokes ready,

21
00:02:00,182 --> 00:02:05,310
but if you ask me if she’s funny…

22
00:02:09,929 --> 00:02:10,997
that is a…

23
00:02:13,399 --> 00:02:15,668
I like it! We can market that!

24
00:02:15,702 --> 00:02:16,744
Yes!

25
00:02:16,769 --> 00:02:17,745
We got this, Mom.

26
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:20,840
Wait, wait, you have to let
your dad know about this, okay?

27
00:02:22,242 --> 00:02:25,879
Yeah, but I think we
should solidify the idea

28
00:02:25,912 --> 00:02:30,383
first, so, you know, Dad
can’t poke any holes in it.

29
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:32,252
Unless it’s a donut.

30
00:02:35,722 --> 00:02:38,858
Like they say, “like father, like son.”

31
00:02:41,861 --> 00:02:44,364
Use “vampire” in a sentence.

32
00:02:44,797 --> 00:02:47,534
If you were a vampire, I’d let you bite me.

33
00:02:47,901 --> 00:02:50,837
We’d still be a perfect match
even if you were a vampire.

34
00:02:51,037 --> 00:02:54,407
Hmm, okay, okay. But
here’s the right one—

35
00:02:55,041 --> 00:02:56,536
Lend me some money, will you?

36
00:02:57,510 --> 00:02:59,479
Do you have money?

37
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:06,219
His jokes? Not for me.

38
00:03:06,586 --> 00:03:09,022
Because his jokes—only
he understands them.

39
00:03:10,924 --> 00:03:12,371
Kind of like me, right?

40
00:03:13,459 --> 00:03:16,095
I made a joke just now, and
you guys didn’t get it, right?

41
00:03:16,959 --> 00:03:17,972
Nothing.

42
00:03:20,166 --> 00:03:24,037
As for Atasha, I would
say she’s very opinionated.

43
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:28,637
She always has a
solution for every problem.

44
00:03:29,286 --> 00:03:37,717
So, the idea is, we’ll have a weekly
event to develop a habit among customers.

45
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:38,860
Okay?

46
00:03:38,887 --> 00:03:40,051
Very smart.

47
00:03:40,853 --> 00:03:45,024
She’s like me, but… very talkative.

48
00:03:45,592 --> 00:03:51,497
You know, when she was a
baby, I used to pray to God that

49
00:03:51,631 --> 00:03:53,166
she’d start talking already

50
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:56,302
because I was so excited to
have conversations with her.

51
00:03:57,203 --> 00:04:02,200
And you know what? At just two months
old—yes, two months!—she started talking.

52
00:04:02,241 --> 00:04:09,115
And since then, even in her
sleep, she never stops talking!

53
00:04:09,148 --> 00:04:10,450
- MPox?!
- MPox?!

54
00:04:10,850 --> 00:04:12,318
Do I have MPox?!

55
00:04:15,622 --> 00:04:20,593
For example, we can have a
Senior Bonding Day every Sunday.

56
00:04:20,627 --> 00:04:21,694
How about this?

57
00:04:22,128 --> 00:04:24,597
A Speed Dating Event?

58
00:04:24,631 --> 00:04:30,803
When you buy a romantic ensaymada,
one bite, and boom—it’s a match!

59
00:04:32,572 --> 00:04:34,114
Wait, have you had lunch?

60
00:04:34,974 --> 00:04:35,675
Lunch?!

61
00:04:35,708 --> 00:04:36,417
Yes?

62
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:37,785
Oh, I haven’t!

63
00:04:37,810 --> 00:04:40,246
You know, Gina, these
marketing strategies the

64
00:04:40,246 --> 00:04:42,615
clients are requesting,
they’re killing me.

65
00:04:42,649 --> 00:04:46,185
And they want everything done ASAP,
and today, I still have pending projects!

66
00:04:46,219 --> 00:04:49,022
I didn’t get any sleep
last night, my brain is in

67
00:04:49,022 --> 00:04:51,824
overload mode, like OMG,
do I even deserve this?!

68
00:04:51,824 --> 00:04:52,759
And you know what?

69
00:04:52,792 --> 00:04:55,695
My only saving grace is
that I dreamt about my crush—

70
00:04:56,396 --> 00:04:57,297
David!

71
00:04:57,330 --> 00:05:01,434
He was helping me finish my
projects. Isn’t the universe amazing?!

72
00:05:06,305 --> 00:05:08,975
He has a big heart, he’s
helpful, and he’s forgiving!

73
00:05:09,008 --> 00:05:12,612
But when he has a problem, he doesn’t
want to ask us for help. He’s too shy!

74
00:05:12,745 --> 00:05:14,547
But you know, that’s our family.

75
00:05:14,614 --> 00:05:16,149
He says he’s a problem solver.

76
00:05:20,887 --> 00:05:21,754
This isn’t right.

77
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:24,070
This isn’t right.

78
00:05:24,624 --> 00:05:26,359
How am I supposed to save money like this?

79
00:05:28,294 --> 00:05:30,563
The ingredients are
way too expensive.

80
00:05:31,064 --> 00:05:32,732
I’ll barely break even.

81
00:05:32,765 --> 00:05:36,969
And if I’m just breaking even,
my expenses are in danger again.

82
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:41,507
How am I supposed to pay off
our debts? That’s what I’m saying.

83
00:05:41,541 --> 00:05:44,677
What’s more important
than these gimmicks is

84
00:05:44,711 --> 00:05:47,847
making sure the product
is actually good.

85
00:05:48,247 --> 00:05:52,485
The gimmicks are great, sure,
but the product has to come first.

86
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:54,787
Because what’s the
point of having all these

87
00:05:54,821 --> 00:05:57,123
marketing tricks if the
product itself is bad?

88
00:05:57,657 --> 00:05:58,524
It’s useless.

89
00:05:58,549 --> 00:05:59,959
I’m sorry, Miss Goldie!

90
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:00,460
- Again!
- Sorry!

91
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:02,428
That’s enough! That’s enough!

92
00:06:03,429 --> 00:06:04,764
Dad, Dad! Dad, relax!

93
00:06:05,331 --> 00:06:06,632
The customer is always right!

94
00:06:06,666 --> 00:06:08,668
No, no! Not in this situation!

95
00:06:09,202 --> 00:06:11,704
My child has already apologized multiple
times, and you’re still humiliating them?

96
00:06:12,138 --> 00:06:14,140
What if I humiliate your whole family?

97
00:06:14,574 --> 00:06:17,610
What if I write a review and
get your business shut down?!

98
00:06:17,744 --> 00:06:19,035
Go ahead!

99
00:06:19,078 --> 00:06:22,682
Shut down our bakery, I
don’t care! No problem!

100
00:06:22,915 --> 00:06:25,218
But you can’t humiliate my child like that!

101
00:06:25,384 --> 00:06:28,921
What happened was an accident! The way
you’re talking, you’re just being cruel!

102
00:06:28,988 --> 00:06:30,356
- Pandesal de Balloon?
- Dad!

103
00:06:31,324 --> 00:06:32,355
What?!

104
00:06:32,959 --> 00:06:34,827
Uh… Andres has something to say.

105
00:06:34,861 --> 00:06:35,495
Uh… uh…

106
00:06:35,528 --> 00:06:37,074
- What is it?!
- Keep up the good work.

107
00:06:38,831 --> 00:06:40,666
Yeah, Dad’s strict.

108
00:06:40,967 --> 00:06:42,935
Actually, I look just like him.

109
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:45,338
Finally, I’m seeing you, wow!

110
00:06:45,872 --> 00:06:48,975
I’ve seen this before, huh?

111
00:06:49,342 --> 00:06:50,738
Just like a dad.

112
00:06:50,777 --> 00:06:54,981
At first, he treats you like a friend,
and then… well, you know.

113
00:07:07,693 --> 00:07:10,496
Looks like you’re trying
to seduce my niece, huh?

114
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:11,697
Interesting move.

115
00:07:11,731 --> 00:07:12,165
Orb—

116
00:07:12,198 --> 00:07:14,901
You’re pulling an Aga move, huh?

117
00:07:15,735 --> 00:07:16,936
No comment.

118
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:24,410
He's very romantic, that's
why I fell in love with him.

119
00:07:26,212 --> 00:07:27,313
Of course, I love you!

120
00:07:27,947 --> 00:07:29,849
You're so thoughtful, my love!

121
00:07:30,149 --> 00:07:33,753
I really thought you
forgot our anniversary!

122
00:07:35,087 --> 00:07:36,189
But you didn't!

123
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:40,159
You know, my dream
in life is simple – for us

124
00:07:40,193 --> 00:07:43,095
to be comfortable, to
eat three times a day,

125
00:07:43,396 --> 00:07:45,731
for the kids to be happy,
for you to be happy.

126
00:07:46,098 --> 00:07:48,835
That's all I want. And
we'll make that happen.

127
00:07:49,068 --> 00:07:54,040
That's my dream for
our family too, my love.

128
00:07:55,408 --> 00:07:58,945
I'm sorry, I'll make it
up to you, I promise.

129
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:00,880
- No making up for it!
- Hmm?

130
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:05,418
When you're wrong, you're wrong! Like Chef
K says, every mistake has a punishment!

131
00:08:05,518 --> 00:08:06,619
- So come on…
- Oh?

132
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:07,286
Come on.

133
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,288
- Here?
- Come on, don’t–

134
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:12,192
You, huh?

135
00:08:12,758 --> 00:08:15,194
I’m not used to this! It feels–

136
00:08:15,228 --> 00:08:16,796
Oh, come on, one more! Kiss me here!

137
00:08:16,963 --> 00:08:18,598
Don’t surprise me like that!

138
00:08:18,865 --> 00:08:20,666
- So, are we good now?
- There we go!

139
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:21,701
- Huh?
- Of course!

140
00:08:21,734 --> 00:08:23,169
- Alright, I’m gonna shower.
- You're gonna shower?

141
00:08:23,202 --> 00:08:24,317
Yes.

142
00:08:24,537 --> 00:08:26,939
Okay, bye, my love! We're good now!

143
00:08:27,139 --> 00:08:28,382
Sha-sha...shower?

144
00:08:28,407 --> 00:08:37,250
If there's Miss World, Miss Earth,
and Miss Universe, then what are you?

145
00:08:37,550 --> 00:08:38,583
What?

146
00:08:39,085 --> 00:08:40,208
Someone I miss.

147
00:08:47,493 --> 00:08:48,419
My love…

148
00:08:49,595 --> 00:08:50,630
Hey!

149
00:08:50,630 --> 00:08:52,465
Don't catch me off guard like that!

150
00:08:52,498 --> 00:08:53,966
Come on, let’s eat!

151
00:08:55,301 --> 00:08:57,036
Thank you, thank you, thank you, thank you!

152
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:05,044
But when I get mad at him, all it
takes is one look, and he knows.

153
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:06,412
Is this place nice?

154
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,447
I don’t know.

155
00:09:08,514 --> 00:09:12,051
Sometimes, I think I
just wanna go to a spa.

156
00:09:12,084 --> 00:09:12,660
Huh?

157
00:09:12,685 --> 00:09:14,462
Yeah! I wanna go there.

158
00:09:14,487 --> 00:09:15,054
You’re going there?

159
00:09:15,087 --> 00:09:15,922
Yeah, why not?

160
00:09:16,289 --> 00:09:17,189
Don't!

161
00:09:17,214 --> 00:09:18,249
No!

162
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:19,725
That’s not for you!

163
00:09:19,859 --> 00:09:21,360
- You’ve got a wife and kids!
- Right!

164
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:24,230
I’m not gonna do
anything–just getting a massage!

165
00:09:24,497 --> 00:09:26,465
- Ate Cha's gonna be mad at you.
- Oh, come on!

166
00:09:26,465 --> 00:09:27,466
How would she be mad?

167
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,634
She can’t get mad at me.

168
00:09:28,668 --> 00:09:30,570
I'm the king here, I make the rules!

169
00:09:31,304 --> 00:09:32,276
That’s me!

170
00:09:32,538 --> 00:09:38,477
Whatever I say, they trust
me, I’ll do it, and I’ll pay for it!

171
00:09:38,511 --> 00:09:40,379
- That’s you, huh?
- That’s really me!

172
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:41,681
Hmm? What did you say?

173
00:09:43,516 --> 00:09:44,884
Uh-oh. That’s you, huh?

174
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:46,519
- My love…
- Mmm? What did you say?

175
00:09:47,019 --> 00:09:47,929
Nothing.

176
00:09:47,954 --> 00:09:50,656
Sometimes, I just wanna
bang my head against a wall.

177
00:09:52,591 --> 00:09:53,481
I don’t know anymore.

178
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,090
Right?

179
00:09:55,661 --> 00:09:56,404
One more.

180
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:57,363
Nothing. Really.

181
00:09:57,396 --> 00:09:59,365
- Did you say something?
- I didn’t say anything. I said–

182
00:09:59,398 --> 00:10:00,833
- You’re the best.
- Alright.

183
00:10:01,367 --> 00:10:02,835
One more. Say it.

184
00:10:03,469 --> 00:10:04,579
- Nothing.
- I’m the best?

185
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:05,696
Yes, totally. Super.

186
00:10:06,639 --> 00:10:07,673
Okay, very good.

187
00:10:11,877 --> 00:10:13,079
She taught us a lot of things.

188
00:10:13,179 --> 00:10:15,381
For example, how many islands
are there in the Philippines?

189
00:10:15,681 --> 00:10:18,217
It depends—high tide or low tide?

190
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:21,220
And she’s the perfect wife to our
Dad, the perfect Mom to our family,

191
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:24,523
perfect beauty and
brains, perfect neighbor.

192
00:10:25,358 --> 00:10:27,259
Mom, Dad has a card!

193
00:10:27,326 --> 00:10:28,367
- Huh?
- Look!

194
00:10:30,229 --> 00:10:39,271
<i>I appreciate your effort. Thank you,
Tash, Andres, and to you, my loving Cha.</i>

195
00:10:42,341 --> 00:10:44,910
You know, this is a good start.

196
00:10:45,211 --> 00:10:46,512
Baby steps.

197
00:10:46,946 --> 00:10:51,083
Little by little, your Dad
will learn to ask for help.

198
00:10:52,385 --> 00:10:54,420
Pride has no place
in the Pers family.

199
00:10:54,453 --> 00:10:55,296
Yeah.

200
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:59,270
I understand they just want to help,

201
00:10:59,458 --> 00:11:02,561
and they’re trying to find ways to do
it, and there’s nothing wrong with that.

202
00:11:03,029 --> 00:11:07,466
But I just feel like there should be
one person making the decisions.

203
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,404
So, I don’t mind them helping,
I’m not saying it’s wrong,

204
00:11:11,437 --> 00:11:14,535
but who’s really in charge here at home?

205
00:11:14,974 --> 00:11:18,010
They’re scared to even
ask for your permission.

206
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:20,004
Whose side are you on?

207
00:11:20,146 --> 00:11:22,035
There’s no sides.

208
00:11:22,815 --> 00:11:24,183
We’re one team.

209
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:33,359
But in every dish or
recipe we make, no matter

210
00:11:33,392 --> 00:11:39,231
how small, every
ingredient has a contribution—

211
00:11:39,265 --> 00:11:40,299
it’s important!

212
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:43,269
If even one
ingredient is missing,

213
00:11:44,003 --> 00:11:47,606
the taste and appearance
change completely.

214
00:11:49,775 --> 00:11:53,913
But they added fruit to the ensaymada.

215
00:11:54,013 --> 00:11:54,847
Mm-hmm.

216
00:11:55,347 --> 00:12:00,653
But did it ruin the taste, or
did it make it even better?

217
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:11,964
You know, Atasha, Andres, you’ve
helped me and your Dad so much.

218
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:20,806
So whatever decision
you make, we’ll support it.

219
00:12:22,541 --> 00:12:23,651
Thanks, Mom.

220
00:12:23,676 --> 00:12:24,744
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

221
00:12:37,256 --> 00:12:39,125
Oh, okay!

222
00:12:39,525 --> 00:12:43,158
- We love you, my love!
- We love you, Dad!

223
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:47,733
Okay, lower it a bit. There, there.

224
00:12:55,708 --> 00:12:58,377
Ow. Hey, Charity, take it easy.

225
00:13:00,813 --> 00:13:03,015
So, how's the pressure, Kuya Aga?

226
00:13:03,048 --> 00:13:07,019
A little strong, maybe
ease up a bit, but it's okay.

227
00:13:08,254 --> 00:13:10,556
Oh wow, this is really how I do massages.

228
00:13:11,657 --> 00:13:13,959
Classic Charity. Whoo!

229
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:15,928
Is this okay?

230
00:13:16,028 --> 00:13:19,398
Yaaaa–ouch! Ouch, ouch, ouch!

231
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:27,606
Ow, my god! It’s
like–Charity…that’s hitting deep.

232
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:28,917
How–

233
00:13:29,141 --> 00:13:31,076
This is a new technique!

234
00:13:31,076 --> 00:13:33,112
This feels just like my wife!

235
00:13:33,112 --> 00:13:34,847
She massages me like this!

236
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,950
Sometimes I even get
mad when she does it.

237
00:13:38,350 --> 00:13:40,519
But since it’s you, it’s fine, go ahead!

238
00:13:42,354 --> 00:13:43,756
Whoo, Charity!

239
00:13:44,623 --> 00:13:47,560
Charity, can I get your phone number?

240
00:13:48,093 --> 00:13:50,095
I’ll just take it later after this.

241
00:13:50,129 --> 00:13:50,830
Uh…

242
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,565
- Is that okay?
- Sure.

243
00:13:52,598 --> 00:13:54,066
No, just in case…you know.

244
00:13:54,066 --> 00:13:55,935
If I need to text you sometimes,

245
00:13:56,235 --> 00:14:01,240
if…you know, in case you ever
need anything, maybe I can help.

246
00:14:01,607 --> 00:14:06,712
Oh, and you can also give me your
account number if–ow! Your account number.

247
00:14:06,712 --> 00:14:09,548
What account number
nonsense are you talking about?!

248
00:14:09,615 --> 00:14:11,016
- Accou–like…
- Huh?!

249
00:14:11,450 --> 00:14:13,652
Even your voice is starting
to sound like my wife!

250
00:14:15,321 --> 00:14:16,021
Wow.

251
00:14:16,255 --> 00:14:17,656
So, what’s your account number?

252
00:14:17,756 --> 00:14:18,324
What?!

253
00:14:18,490 --> 00:14:20,793
You’re saying it again?! Account number?!

254
00:14:21,093 --> 00:14:22,428
What are you talking about?!

255
00:14:22,895 --> 00:14:24,129
She sounds just like my wife!

256
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:27,066
Just like?! Look at me!

257
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:28,000
My love!

258
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:31,303
Oh, what?! What are you doing here?!

259
00:14:31,337 --> 00:14:33,105
What are you doing here?!

260
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:34,740
- Wh-why is this happening?!
- What are you doing here?!

261
00:14:34,773 --> 00:14:38,010
Charity! Charity, you–huh?!

262
00:14:38,911 --> 00:14:39,712
Gets?

263
00:14:47,186 --> 00:14:48,387
We're best friends, Aga and I.

264
00:14:49,521 --> 00:14:50,456
We're close!

265
00:14:51,090 --> 00:14:52,258
We're good!

266
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:53,893
Really good!

267
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:58,898
What do you have that
made my Chacha fall for you?

268
00:14:59,398 --> 00:14:59,798
What?

269
00:14:59,798 --> 00:15:00,699
Your Chacha.

270
00:15:01,300 --> 00:15:02,501
Yours. That’s what I said.

271
00:15:03,202 --> 00:15:04,402
Why is that?

272
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:05,379
Let me see.

273
00:15:06,171 --> 00:15:10,342
Oh... you do have something!
Is it the dreamy eyes?

274
00:15:12,311 --> 00:15:13,479
Here, let me check.

275
00:15:13,712 --> 00:15:16,048
Oh wow, red lips!

276
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:18,984
Mmm, dimples!

277
00:15:20,819 --> 00:15:23,289
Oh, double chin!

278
00:15:23,489 --> 00:15:24,590
I have that too!

279
00:15:24,890 --> 00:15:28,727
If anyone says we're
not okay, it's not true!

280
00:15:29,028 --> 00:15:31,931
Why would I hold a grudge
against my best friend—

281
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:34,133
the one who stole my date back then?

282
00:15:34,667 --> 00:15:39,038
So, does that mean our date is off?

283
00:15:39,071 --> 00:15:40,005
No, no, no!

284
00:15:40,306 --> 00:15:42,174
I already called my best friend, okay?

285
00:15:42,374 --> 00:15:43,776
My forever best friend.

286
00:15:44,009 --> 00:15:48,380
He'll keep you company for
a while, but Cha, I'll catch up.

287
00:15:49,348 --> 00:15:50,357
Okay.

288
00:15:54,353 --> 00:15:56,322
Bro! Bro, bro, bro, bro!

289
00:15:57,990 --> 00:15:59,325
Come on!

290
00:15:59,825 --> 00:16:00,826
You're unbelievable!

291
00:16:00,859 --> 00:16:03,662
You're already ugly, and
your timing is terrible too!

292
00:16:03,896 --> 00:16:05,764
What's wrong with you? Come here!

293
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:06,732
Sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry!

294
00:16:06,732 --> 00:16:08,300
Bro, it was right there!

295
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:10,869
Just an inch away, and
it would've been a smack!

296
00:16:10,936 --> 00:16:13,172
- I know! But I didn't mean to—
- You're hopeless!

297
00:16:13,172 --> 00:16:14,940
I said I'm sorry! My bad, bro!

298
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:16,575
I'm really sorry!

299
00:16:22,269 --> 00:16:23,132
Uh…

300
00:16:25,351 --> 00:16:26,358
Hi.

301
00:16:26,719 --> 00:16:27,686
Hi.

302
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,430
I’m Aga.

303
00:16:29,455 --> 00:16:31,323
- I’m Charlene.
- Charlene.

304
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:39,873
Nice to meet you.

305
00:16:39,898 --> 00:16:41,166
Nice to meet you!

306
00:16:46,839 --> 00:16:48,707
Ouch! Ow!

307
00:16:48,707 --> 00:16:51,143
- Dude!
- Bro!

308
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:55,080
Don’t electrify her! Stay out of this, man!

309
00:16:55,114 --> 00:16:58,083
- I'm really sorry!
- Just step aside, come on!

310
00:16:58,117 --> 00:16:59,351
Sorry, sorry.

311
00:16:59,385 --> 00:17:00,853
You're getting on my nerves.

312
00:17:00,886 --> 00:17:01,987
That was ages ago!

313
00:17:02,588 --> 00:17:03,722
Let’s move on!

314
00:17:04,289 --> 00:17:05,758
Past is past!

315
00:17:06,925 --> 00:17:07,960
My condolences.

316
00:17:07,993 --> 00:17:08,460
Shut it!

317
00:17:08,494 --> 00:17:09,828
- My condolences!
- Condolences, Chef!

318
00:17:13,532 --> 00:17:14,566
Who died?

319
00:17:16,402 --> 00:17:21,473
It's the death anniversary of
my heart, which you broke, Aga.

320
00:17:22,841 --> 00:17:24,076
But remember this—

321
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:27,513
I will make sure that as long as I live,

322
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:29,982
you will be miserable

323
00:17:30,682 --> 00:17:35,054
and will never feel true
happiness in your life.

324
00:17:41,226 --> 00:17:43,862
So, are we switching suppliers?

325
00:17:45,030 --> 00:17:47,699
That could be great, my love—it's cheaper.

326
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,502
But when you factor in shipping,

327
00:17:51,336 --> 00:17:53,305
it evens out, still expensive.

328
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:54,656
Unbelievable!

329
00:17:55,229 --> 00:17:56,547
This is what I hate the most!

330
00:17:57,176 --> 00:17:59,211
I try to help, and somehow,
I end up being the bad guy!

331
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:00,946
You know what, let's just
settle this with a fistfight!

332
00:18:00,979 --> 00:18:02,281
- BFF!
- Chef, chef!

333
00:18:02,281 --> 00:18:04,235
Whoever wins gets Charlene! Ha!

334
00:18:05,350 --> 00:18:07,519
Wha—why are you so mad?!
Who are you even angry at?

335
00:18:07,519 --> 00:18:08,487
I'm really pissed off!

336
00:18:08,487 --> 00:18:09,721
At who?!

337
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:10,664
The supplier.

338
00:18:10,823 --> 00:18:11,790
Oh, okay.

339
00:18:11,790 --> 00:18:12,925
I'm mad at him.

340
00:18:13,525 --> 00:18:20,032
I'm the one giving him business, giving
him a profit, and he won't even adjust?

341
00:18:20,332 --> 00:18:21,428
What does he think?

342
00:18:21,867 --> 00:18:23,569
I'm seriously getting irritated!

343
00:18:23,802 --> 00:18:24,803
I just want to punch him!

344
00:18:24,837 --> 00:18:25,737
Who exactly?!

345
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:26,796
The supplier!

346
00:18:27,005 --> 00:18:31,243
I want to punch him. I'm so annoyed!

347
00:18:31,343 --> 00:18:33,779
Your debt—pay it! Now!

348
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:35,314
Have mercy on me!

349
00:18:35,681 --> 00:18:36,715
Mercy?

350
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:37,728
Yes!

351
00:18:38,650 --> 00:18:45,457
Did you feel that "mercy"
when you stole Chacha from me?

352
00:18:47,259 --> 00:18:48,360
Did you feel it?

353
00:18:48,927 --> 00:18:53,232
Do you think I’m going to
let you off the hook when you

354
00:18:53,265 --> 00:18:58,136
didn’t even feel an ounce of
mercy for what you did to me?

355
00:18:59,505 --> 00:19:00,592
Mercy?!

356
00:19:00,617 --> 00:19:01,639
What mercy?!

357
00:19:03,342 --> 00:19:08,313
Wait, wait, hold on. This sounds
serious. What's going on between you two?

358
00:19:08,347 --> 00:19:08,814
Chacha!

359
00:19:08,847 --> 00:19:09,915
- Ah, yes?
- Ah..

360
00:19:09,915 --> 00:19:12,651
No, it's just... he's
asking me to pay my debt.

361
00:19:12,818 --> 00:19:13,385
Huh?

362
00:19:13,485 --> 00:19:16,555
What?! You're up to something again!

363
00:19:16,588 --> 00:19:17,623
What's going on in your head?!

364
00:19:17,890 --> 00:19:20,192
I never said I was
asking for money!

365
00:19:20,225 --> 00:19:23,395
I was just passing by, Chacha, and he
suddenly got all worked up about his debt.

366
00:19:23,395 --> 00:19:25,797
I told him, "Don't worry
about it. Bro, relax."

367
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:27,399
What do you mean "don't
worry about it"? Why?

368
00:19:27,399 --> 00:19:30,369
I mean, don’t think about it now—you
can just pay at the end of the month.

369
00:19:31,637 --> 00:19:35,073
Ah, Chef K, you're the
best! Thank you so much!

370
00:19:36,041 --> 00:19:39,711
Chacha, but it still hurts,
you know? He yelled at me.

371
00:19:39,745 --> 00:19:40,379
Huh?

372
00:19:40,746 --> 00:19:42,347
- I didn’t—
- You yelled at him?

373
00:19:42,381 --> 00:19:44,016
- I yelled at you?!
- Huh? Don’t—

374
00:19:44,049 --> 00:19:45,617
I just wish he wouldn’t yell at me.

375
00:19:45,651 --> 00:19:46,585
He's the one asking me to pay my debt.

376
00:19:46,618 --> 00:19:48,654
- Don’t yell at him, my love!
- I didn’t!

377
00:19:49,254 --> 00:19:50,455
Wow! Supplies?

378
00:19:50,455 --> 00:19:52,925
What do you think
this is, a delivery van?

379
00:19:52,958 --> 00:19:55,961
- Yes!
- Wow, ang ganda naman nito!

380
00:19:55,994 --> 00:19:57,496
- Don't touch it, Ate Cha!
- Don't touch it!

381
00:19:57,896 --> 00:20:01,233
- It's so fancy!
- Don’t—my love, don’t touch it!

382
00:20:01,266 --> 00:20:03,368
Not just that, look at the lights. Oh.

383
00:20:03,635 --> 00:20:05,704
Oh, Kuya, but you're
letting Ate Cha touch it.

384
00:20:05,737 --> 00:20:07,739
The car is so nice! I really want to—

385
00:20:07,973 --> 00:20:08,777
My love!

386
00:20:11,476 --> 00:20:12,778
Oh, why are you laughing?

387
00:20:12,811 --> 00:20:13,979
We should test drive it!

388
00:20:14,012 --> 00:20:17,683
Great acting there, Pokwang!

389
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:19,512
Oh, one more time, one more time!

390
00:20:21,119 --> 00:20:22,921
My love, my love, my love!

391
00:20:22,955 --> 00:20:23,322
What?

392
00:20:23,355 --> 00:20:26,258
You're the only one allowed to hug it!
You’re the only one allowed to touch it!

393
00:20:26,291 --> 00:20:28,961
- Then we should definitely test drive it!
- Oh!

394
00:20:28,961 --> 00:20:30,896
Perfect timing, Chef K…

395
00:20:31,129 --> 00:20:31,463
Oh?

396
00:20:31,496 --> 00:20:35,300
My love needs to pick up some
supplies. Maybe you could go with him?

397
00:20:35,334 --> 00:20:36,001
He doesn’t want to!

398
00:20:36,034 --> 00:20:36,977
See, I told you!

399
00:20:37,002 --> 00:20:38,737
That’s exactly what I
said! He doesn’t want to!

400
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:39,238
Huh?

401
00:20:39,271 --> 00:20:42,407
I've been telling him I’d be
the one to deliver the supplies!

402
00:20:42,441 --> 00:20:44,710
- You just said you didn’t want to!
- I never said that! Come on, just say yes.

403
00:20:44,843 --> 00:20:46,178
- So, are we getting it?
- Before I change my mind.

404
00:20:46,211 --> 00:20:47,913
- Oh, never mind, let’s just go.
- Okay.

405
00:20:48,447 --> 00:20:51,216
What’s this about asking for
an account number, my love?!

406
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:51,850
Account num—

407
00:20:51,883 --> 00:20:53,585
- And a phone number?!
- My love, you don’t—

408
00:20:54,119 --> 00:20:55,120
- Hey!
- Hey!

409
00:20:55,153 --> 00:20:55,621
BFF!

410
00:20:55,654 --> 00:20:56,663
That’s what I like to see!

411
00:20:56,688 --> 00:20:58,590
- Good thing you showed up!
- Oh really?

412
00:20:58,624 --> 00:21:00,292
- Yes!
- What are you doing here?!

413
00:21:00,325 --> 00:21:02,928
I was gonna ask if you were already
fighting. So, are you breaking up?

414
00:21:03,128 --> 00:21:04,696
- No!
- No. But…

415
00:21:04,730 --> 00:21:05,864
- Why would we break up?
- Yeah!

416
00:21:05,897 --> 00:21:08,033
What do you mean "no"? Look at you two—

417
00:21:08,066 --> 00:21:09,368
- Not happening!
- Did he even ask your permission?

418
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,603
You guys are impossible!
You’re so hard to break apart!

419
00:21:11,637 --> 00:21:12,604
Thank you so much, Chef K.

420
00:21:13,872 --> 00:21:16,441
Promise, I won’t tell.

421
00:21:18,176 --> 00:21:19,444
Come on, it’s you!

422
00:21:20,846 --> 00:21:22,581
I don’t even know why
you’re putting up with that.

423
00:21:22,914 --> 00:21:24,716
Huh? What did you say?

424
00:21:24,850 --> 00:21:26,318
Ah, nothing!

425
00:21:27,019 --> 00:21:29,988
I said… why are
you so beautiful?

426
00:21:31,390 --> 00:21:33,125
You’re so sweet, thank you, Chef!

427
00:21:37,929 --> 00:21:39,164
Anything for you!

428
00:21:39,231 --> 00:21:40,432
Thank you, thanks!

429
00:21:40,699 --> 00:21:41,686
Thank you!

430
00:21:42,267 --> 00:21:47,472
Actually, the first time our eyes
met, wow, I could totally read it!

431
00:21:48,473 --> 00:21:51,643
It was like she was
begging me to court her.

432
00:22:18,704 --> 00:22:19,717
What happened?!

433
00:22:23,775 --> 00:22:24,776
Where am I?!

434
00:22:32,818 --> 00:22:33,697
Hey!

435
00:22:35,053 --> 00:22:35,916
It’s me!

436
00:22:36,822 --> 00:22:37,830
It’s really me!

437
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:42,088
What happened?!

438
00:22:42,327 --> 00:22:43,528
Am I in a hospital?!

439
00:22:43,895 --> 00:22:46,231
Good morning, my love!

440
00:22:47,165 --> 00:22:48,500
Good morning!

441
00:22:49,267 --> 00:22:50,291
Oh no!

442
00:22:50,635 --> 00:22:51,803
I’m not in a hospital!

443
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:54,072
Where am I?!

444
00:22:55,607 --> 00:22:56,603
Am I in heaven?!

445
00:22:57,976 --> 00:22:58,986
What?!

446
00:22:59,511 --> 00:23:00,645
Am I dead?!

447
00:23:00,846 --> 00:23:02,547
What are you even saying, Karl?!

448
00:23:02,881 --> 00:23:03,949
Dead?!

449
00:23:05,250 --> 00:23:08,854
But me – I’m dead in love with you!

450
00:23:09,521 --> 00:23:11,356
Hey, Cha! Cha, wait…hold on, hold on!

451
00:23:11,356 --> 00:23:12,324
Calm down!

452
00:23:13,458 --> 00:23:18,430
I know you can’t resist me, but what
we’re doing is wrong. This is forbidden!

453
00:23:18,530 --> 00:23:18,830
Huh?!

454
00:23:18,864 --> 00:23:20,699
We’re cheating on Aga!

455
00:23:20,732 --> 00:23:22,000
- What?!
- Yes!

456
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,770
Karl, I’m your wife!

457
00:23:26,638 --> 00:23:28,039
What are you talking about?!

458
00:23:37,582 --> 00:23:39,050
- And this too.
- Can I have a bread?

459
00:23:39,384 --> 00:23:39,751
That’s it.

460
00:23:39,785 --> 00:23:42,721
- Can I have a bread?
- Yeah! You got it. Okay…

461
00:23:43,922 --> 00:23:44,956
Can you get the…?

462
00:23:45,123 --> 00:23:45,590
What?

463
00:23:45,624 --> 00:23:46,158
Oh!

464
00:23:46,525 --> 00:23:48,059
Oh! Hi, Dad!

465
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:49,261
- Dad!
- Good morning!

466
00:23:49,294 --> 00:23:52,097
- Good morning, Dad!
- Good morning, good morning!

467
00:23:52,130 --> 00:23:53,507
- Good morning!
- Good morning, Dad!

468
00:23:53,532 --> 00:23:54,566
How was your sleep?

469
00:23:57,369 --> 00:23:58,400
I’m your dad?

470
00:23:58,870 --> 00:23:59,604
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

471
00:23:59,671 --> 00:24:00,539
Of course!

472
00:24:00,705 --> 00:24:03,575
Unless you’re trying to tell us…

473
00:24:04,876 --> 00:24:06,611
we’re adopted?!

474
00:24:06,645 --> 00:24:07,946
- Adopted?! Adop–
- No…no…

475
00:24:08,947 --> 00:24:10,415
–Tash, what are you saying?!

476
00:24:10,482 --> 00:24:11,650
- That’s impossible!
- Dad!

477
00:24:12,250 --> 00:24:15,253
Tash, look! Tash! Hey! Hey, Tash!

478
00:24:15,754 --> 00:24:17,222
We look exactly alike, see?!

479
00:24:18,390 --> 00:24:19,024
Right?!

480
00:24:19,057 --> 00:24:21,293
- At least the nose, yeah!
- Oh! Yeah!

481
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:23,895
But wait, now I’m even more confused!

482
00:24:24,362 --> 00:24:24,996
Why?!

483
00:24:25,030 --> 00:24:27,999
Oh no, no, no! Come on!

484
00:24:28,233 --> 00:24:32,704
You’re even the first one
to get amnesia before me!

485
00:24:32,737 --> 00:24:33,738
Karl!

486
00:24:34,706 --> 00:24:36,942
Why? What am I supposed to remember?

487
00:24:37,509 --> 00:24:42,047
That you’re the head of this
family, and you own the bakery.

488
00:24:43,715 --> 00:24:46,785
So that means I own all of this?

489
00:24:46,885 --> 00:24:49,254
- Oh, but of course!
- Yeah!

490
00:24:49,321 --> 00:24:51,623
It’s like… I switched lives with Aga.

491
00:24:52,023 --> 00:24:53,592
We switched lives!

492
00:25:07,405 --> 00:25:10,141
Haters gonna hate! Right?

493
00:25:10,141 --> 00:25:10,642
Exactly!

494
00:25:10,709 --> 00:25:15,247
But of course, I get it.
You’re jealous because

495
00:25:15,614 --> 00:25:20,986
my love and I are happy
together, and you’re still single.

496
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:23,989
Single!

497
00:25:24,022 --> 00:25:24,623
You call that happiness?!

498
00:25:24,656 --> 00:25:26,691
Where’s your—what is this?!

499
00:25:26,992 --> 00:25:30,161
This is what you’re so
proud of?! Wait a minute…

500
00:25:30,629 --> 00:25:31,630
Honeybunch!

501
00:25:31,630 --> 00:25:34,866
Yes?! Yes! I’m here!

502
00:25:36,968 --> 00:25:39,304
Oh! Is this Karl and Cha?

503
00:25:39,337 --> 00:25:40,872
- Yes!
- Hi!

504
00:25:40,906 --> 00:25:43,975
Nice to meet you! I’ve heard
so many good things about you!

505
00:25:44,009 --> 00:25:47,846
- Wow! Wow!
- Nice to meet you!

506
00:25:47,879 --> 00:25:49,881
- Aga, I’m happy for you!
- Yes!

507
00:25:49,915 --> 00:25:54,386
At least your life will finally be as
sweet as mine and Cha’s! Right? N

508
00:25:54,419 --> 00:25:57,622
o, no way! That’s not sweet at all!
Now, this is really sweet! Look at this!

509
00:25:57,689 --> 00:25:58,823
- Oh no!
- Oh!

510
00:25:59,591 --> 00:26:01,426
- Like this!
- Let’s see!

511
00:26:01,459 --> 00:26:07,799
Don’t meddle in my life, okay?

512
00:26:09,234 --> 00:26:16,408
I run my own life! Got it?

513
00:26:16,541 --> 00:26:19,878
Don’t get on my nerves!

514
00:26:20,745 --> 00:26:21,838
Karl...

515
00:26:22,213 --> 00:26:25,250
Karl, not every day is a happy one.

516
00:26:25,350 --> 00:26:26,126
Oh?

517
00:26:26,151 --> 00:26:27,275
Same for me.

518
00:26:27,652 --> 00:26:30,822
Because I heard you’re having
problems with your family.

519
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:32,963
What?!

520
00:26:33,091 --> 00:26:35,126
- What family problems?!
- Yeah!

521
00:26:35,860 --> 00:26:37,495
Where did you hear that, you gossip?!

522
00:26:37,529 --> 00:26:39,364
I heard it, I’m not gossiping!

523
00:26:39,397 --> 00:26:41,266
You are gossiping! Why are
you meddling in my family—

524
00:26:41,299 --> 00:26:42,367
do you want to just
settle this with a fight?!

525
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:44,369
- I just heard it, I just—
- Hey! Whoa, whoa, whoa!

526
00:26:44,402 --> 00:26:45,637
You’re stepping out of line!

527
00:26:45,670 --> 00:26:47,205
Hep! Hep, hooray!

528
00:26:47,906 --> 00:26:49,674
No violence allowed here.

529
00:26:49,708 --> 00:26:52,911
If you want, just settle it with
a dance showdown! Music!

530
00:26:54,112 --> 00:26:56,247
What dance showdown?!
What are you saying?!

531
00:26:56,681 --> 00:26:57,949
Playing music now?!

532
00:26:58,216 --> 00:26:59,838
I don’t like this kind of thing!

533
00:27:00,085 --> 00:27:01,987
I hate this stuff! Huh?!

534
00:27:01,987 --> 00:27:03,150
- Oh!
- Ah!

535
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:07,559
My kid taught me something, Tash!

536
00:27:08,293 --> 00:27:09,302
That move!

537
00:27:09,335 --> 00:27:10,737
That’s what Tash does!

538
00:27:11,062 --> 00:27:13,331
It’s like that kid is teaching me!

539
00:27:13,509 --> 00:27:14,374
Do it!

540
00:27:14,399 --> 00:27:14,933
Oh wow!

541
00:27:14,966 --> 00:27:16,301
Hi, Karl!

542
00:27:16,768 --> 00:27:17,811
Chacha!

543
00:27:17,836 --> 00:27:19,504
Oh, Chacha!

544
00:27:21,339 --> 00:27:22,674
- Oh!
- Cha!

545
00:27:22,774 --> 00:27:25,210
- I missed you, Karl!
- My Chacha!

546
00:27:25,910 --> 00:27:26,924
Cha!

547
00:27:29,514 --> 00:27:32,417
But no, I can’t say anything.

548
00:27:32,884 --> 00:27:35,620
And besides, I just feel
bad for my best friend, Aga.

549
00:27:36,221 --> 00:27:40,392
Let’s just leave it at that.
After all, I’m happy for them.

550
00:27:41,459 --> 00:27:42,377
Isn’t it obvious?

551
00:27:43,862 --> 00:27:44,775
Huh?

552
00:27:45,478 --> 00:27:47,332
I just want to apologize to you…

553
00:27:48,283 --> 00:27:52,971
and ask for your understanding.

554
00:27:53,705 --> 00:27:55,340
Especially when it comes to Cha.

555
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:59,110
But just know that we
love you. We love you.

556
00:28:01,079 --> 00:28:07,218
That’s why I’m making up for it. Me
too, I don’t like holding onto anger.

557
00:28:08,787 --> 00:28:10,255
BFF, life is short.

558
00:28:10,922 --> 00:28:13,058
I don’t want to fill my
heart with resentment.

559
00:28:13,591 --> 00:28:16,027
That’s exactly what
I’m saying. Life is short.

560
00:28:16,093 --> 00:28:19,266
That’s why I want you
to know that no matter what happens,

561
00:28:19,291 --> 00:28:21,155
as long as we’re alive—

562
00:28:21,466 --> 00:28:28,206
me, my wife, my family—as long
as we’re here, you can count on us.

563
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:30,909
Especially Anne.

564
00:28:32,977 --> 00:28:35,747
We’ll treat Anne like our own child.

565
00:28:36,247 --> 00:28:39,851
That’s what I wanted to hear, BFF!

566
00:28:43,621 --> 00:28:45,723
BFF, give me a hug.

567
00:28:46,391 --> 00:28:48,259
Of course, of course.

568
00:28:49,894 --> 00:28:50,829
Thank you!

569
00:28:51,629 --> 00:28:52,697
Love you, BFF!

570
00:28:52,730 --> 00:28:53,698
Love you, BFF!

571
00:28:53,698 --> 00:28:54,822
Love you. Thank you, okay?

572
00:28:58,136 --> 00:29:02,006
You know, BFF, true friends
always have each other’s backs.

573
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:02,574
Yes!

574
00:29:02,607 --> 00:29:03,883
I can really feel that.

575
00:29:03,908 --> 00:29:06,244
- Yes, yes.
- Huh? Yeah, I know that’s how it is.

576
00:29:06,244 --> 00:29:06,911
Yes, BFF.

577
00:29:06,945 --> 00:29:09,481
You’re the only friend who’s
ever been like this to me.

578
00:29:09,514 --> 00:29:10,815
Don’t disappear on me, okay?

579
00:29:10,849 --> 00:29:12,317
- Okay.
- I’m still taking it all in.

580
00:29:13,618 --> 00:29:14,338
BFF…

581
00:29:15,186 --> 00:29:16,688
I’m savoring the moment.

582
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:20,791
BFF?

583
00:29:22,994 --> 00:29:24,162
What happened?!

584
00:29:24,195 --> 00:29:27,465
You—you got electrocuted! You fainted!

585
00:29:27,599 --> 00:29:28,433
I’m okay now!

586
00:29:28,466 --> 00:29:29,000
You sure?!

587
00:29:29,033 --> 00:29:31,703
Yeah! How long was I—how
many seconds was I gone?!

588
00:29:32,103 --> 00:29:35,006
Just a few seconds, Tso
K. Maybe three seconds.

589
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:36,369
Three seconds?!

590
00:29:36,908 --> 00:29:38,643
It felt like a lifetime!

591
00:29:41,279 --> 00:29:42,314
Just three seconds?!

592
00:29:42,780 --> 00:29:45,116
Oh…you okay now, sis?!

593
00:29:46,951 --> 00:29:48,086
Sis?!

594
00:29:48,386 --> 00:29:51,623
Don’t you “sis” me, you lady!

595
00:29:52,023 --> 00:29:54,225
Can’t you see how macho I am?!

596
00:29:54,359 --> 00:29:55,291
Oh!

597
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:01,399
Look at this bicep! Just the bicep!

598
00:30:01,439 --> 00:30:05,911
Sorry! It’s just… you kinda look like
someone from my past life, you know?

599
00:30:05,937 --> 00:30:07,672
Oh, really?

600
00:30:07,839 --> 00:30:12,243
Miss Marga, he’s definitely not a
“bro”! Look at him—Tso K is pure macho!

601
00:30:12,277 --> 00:30:16,948
Anyway, anyway, looks like everything’s
fine. The grand reopening is back on!

602
00:30:20,385 --> 00:30:23,555
Wait, wait, wait! I need…!

603
00:30:23,888 --> 00:30:28,793
- Water! Water!
- Wait, wait! Water, water?!

604
00:30:28,826 --> 00:30:30,728
I’m good! I’m good. I’m good.

605
00:30:30,762 --> 00:30:34,732
- I’m good! I’m good. I’m good.
- Here, have a drink, Tso K!

606
00:30:40,438 --> 00:30:42,640
Here, have a drink, Tso K!

607
00:30:44,275 --> 00:30:45,252
What the—?!

608
00:30:47,645 --> 00:30:50,348
I didn’t know what to do! I panicked!

609
00:30:50,949 --> 00:30:54,052
Good thing it wasn’t
juice. I’m okay with this.

610
00:30:54,052 --> 00:30:57,504
Alright, Tso K, just rest for a bit, okay?

611
00:30:57,529 --> 00:30:58,565
Rest?

612
00:30:58,590 --> 00:31:00,076
Why would I rest? No way!

613
00:31:00,491 --> 00:31:01,734
Aren’t you giving a speech?

614
00:31:01,759 --> 00:31:03,628
- Oh, right. I have to speak.
- You sure?

615
00:31:03,661 --> 00:31:05,972
- Yeah, yeah!
- You just got electrocuted!

616
00:31:05,997 --> 00:31:06,998
I have to speak!

617
00:31:06,998 --> 00:31:09,107
- Ah, okay…
- Okay… give me the mic.

618
00:31:09,309 --> 00:31:12,846
I have something to say—someone
here is getting exposed!

619
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:13,238
Huh?!

620
00:31:13,238 --> 00:31:15,273
- You all need to know…
- Chef K!

621
00:31:15,306 --> 00:31:16,516
…the truth!

622
00:31:16,541 --> 00:31:18,109
No one can stop me!

623
00:31:18,393 --> 00:31:20,162
I’m telling you, payback is coming!

624
00:31:20,612 --> 00:31:22,814
- No more lies!
- BFF…BFF…

625
00:31:23,781 --> 00:31:26,618
Everybody, listen to me!

626
00:31:27,585 --> 00:31:30,221
This success we’re celebrating?

627
00:31:31,122 --> 00:31:34,058
Aga doesn’t deserve it!

628
00:31:34,525 --> 00:31:35,260
- Huh?!
- Oooohh!

629
00:31:35,293 --> 00:31:36,361
Huh? Why?!

630
00:31:36,494 --> 00:31:37,462
That hurts!

631
00:31:38,596 --> 00:31:44,802
Because you deserve
even more blessings, Aga!

632
00:31:50,308 --> 00:31:54,879
BFF, I know what
you’re going through.

633
00:31:55,280 --> 00:31:59,450
If I were in your shoes, I
don’t think I could handle it.

634
00:32:01,686 --> 00:32:08,126
But you—you worked hard
for everything you have.

635
00:32:10,628 --> 00:32:13,631
You’re an amazing person, BFF!

636
00:32:14,842 --> 00:32:16,000
Congratulations!

637
00:32:18,736 --> 00:32:20,204
Long live, Kuya Aga!

638
00:32:26,377 --> 00:32:30,915
BFF, thank you so, so much. Thank you!

639
00:32:31,249 --> 00:32:32,417
You’re welcome!

640
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:35,453
Let’s give Aga another
big round of applause!

641
00:32:37,195 --> 00:32:40,398
- Congrats, BFF!
- Thank you! Thank you, thank you!

642
00:32:40,425 --> 00:32:44,529
Oh, wait, wait, wait. I also
want to thank all of you…

643
00:32:44,529 --> 00:32:47,231
…because you made our family so happy.

644
00:32:47,231 --> 00:32:48,800
- We’re truly, truly happy.
- Yes!

645
00:32:53,371 --> 00:32:56,441
Let’s say goodbye with a
message for all the moms out there!

646
00:32:56,574 --> 00:33:02,880
Because in problems and
happiness, Pers is first, Pers is the star!

647
00:33:02,914 --> 00:33:08,052
In problems and happiness,
Pers is first, Pers is the star!

648
00:33:11,297 --> 00:33:12,198
That was amazing!

649
00:33:12,223 --> 00:33:14,625
When it comes to problems and happiness…

650
00:33:14,859 --> 00:33:17,028
Pose and post!

651
00:33:18,696 --> 00:33:20,164
Pers is first…

652
00:33:24,881 --> 00:33:27,538
Pers is the star!

653
00:33:30,141 --> 00:33:32,410
In problems and happiness,

654
00:33:34,979 --> 00:33:38,750
Pers is first, Pers is the star!

655
00:33:42,653 --> 00:33:48,226
In problems and happiness,
Pers is first, Pers is the star!
